From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:01:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Time a submarine's ascent to its launch gate

The launcher commands the boat 25.4 ft above the weapon's ceiling but
stops blocking the launch at the ceiling, so the ascent now ends at
GateDepthU when the caller supplies it (default 0 keeps the old
behaviour). A port of the loop puts the Echo II validation run at
49.9 s to the 100 ft ceiling against 58.3 s to 75 ft.

The no-progress bail now counts only while the vertical rate is not
improving: a boat still descending on its tanks used to read as never
arriving, so its launch delay was zero.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CzoHVFmrnnLpRPAqi9LMXe
---
 Simulation/SubmarineAscent.cs | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++------
 docs/model/07-diagnostics.md  | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
